            <ArticleTitle>The outcome of pregnancy following pre-pregnancy or early pregnancy alendronate treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>578-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In spite of a substantial increase in the use of bisphosphonates at child bearing age, very little is known regarding its use in pregnancy. We describe the outcome of 24 pregnancies after pre-pregnancy or early pregnancy alendronate therapy. Based on the pregnancy outcome it seems that alendronate does not impose a major teratogenic risk.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
